# Sage E2E — local config/secrets. Copy to e2e/.env and fill in. e2e/.env is gitignored.

# Base Node.js image to build from (full registry path). Kept out of version control so
# the registry host is not committed. Any Debian-based Node 22 image works; a hardened
# organisational base image is what CI uses.
BASE_IMAGE=<registry-host>/<path>/nodejs:22

# npm registry for the claude/copilot/opencode/vscode Docker builds (they `npm install`
# the agent CLI at build time). Only needed where the public registry is unreachable
# (e.g. on CI); local dev usually doesn't need this. Kept out of version control,
# like BASE_IMAGE.
# NPM_REGISTRY=<registry-host>/api/npm/registry.npmjs.org/

# --- Claude Code (e2e/run.sh claude) — Google Vertex AI backend ---
# Sage E2E authenticates to Claude via Google Vertex AI (NOT the public Anthropic
# API — no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is used in container mode; native mode is the
# exception, see e2e/README.md).
CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=1
ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=<gcp-project-id>   # a GCP project with Vertex AI enabled
CLOUD_ML_REGION=global
# The friendly aliases don't resolve on Vertex, so override what each maps to with a
# model id the project actually serves (verify, e.g. via a rawPredict probe).
# Overriding the aliases lets the suite's default `--model haiku` work as-is.
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5@20251001
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5@20251001
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5@20251001
#
# Auth on Vertex (shared by claude AND opencode):
# - CI/GCE: Google ADC from the agent's attached service account (metadata
#   server) — no key file, no mount; leave SAGE_E2E_GCP_ADC unset.
# - Local (no metadata server): mount this machine's gcloud ADC into the container.
# SAGE_E2E_GCP_ADC=~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json

# --- OpenCode (e2e/run.sh opencode) — also Google Vertex AI ---
# OpenCode is model-agnostic; the container authenticates to Claude via the
# google-vertex-anthropic provider, reusing ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID +
# CLOUD_ML_REGION + the ADC above. Nothing extra needed for the default model.
# Optionally override the model (Vertex model id, default claude-haiku-4-5@20251001):
# OPENCODE_E2E_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5@20251001

# --- Copilot CLI (e2e/run.sh copilot) ---
# A GitHub token with Copilot access. Any of these names works (checked in order
# by the copilot CLI). Copilot uses GitHub-hosted models, so the Vertex vars above
# are irrelevant for it.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-token>
# Optionally override the copilot model (default: claude-haiku-4.5):
# COPILOT_E2E_MODEL=claude-haiku-4.5

# --- Cursor agent CLI (e2e/run.sh cursor) ---
# The Cursor `agent` CLI routes through Cursor's OWN backend (the model alias is
# resolved server-side), so it does NOT use Vertex AI — the Vertex vars above are
# irrelevant for it. Auth is a Cursor API key.
# CURSOR_API_KEY=<your-cursor-api-key>
# Optionally override the model (default: claude-4.5-sonnet):
# SAGE_HEADLESS_AGENT_MODEL=claude-4.5-sonnet

# --- OpenClaw (e2e/run.sh openclaw) — gateway image + Google Vertex AI ---
# OpenClaw ships as a Docker image, not an npm package. Set the image WITHOUT a tag (the
# tag is pinned in e2e/agents.json); the registry host is kept out of version control, like
# BASE_IMAGE. Point this at ghcr.io directly, or at a registry that mirrors it where ghcr.io
# is unreachable — a mirror may prefix the source ref, in which case include that prefix
# here. To bump: make the new tag available, then bump the pin in e2e/agents.json.
# OPENCLAW_IMAGE=ghcr.io/openclaw/openclaw
#
# OpenClaw reaches Gemini through its built-in google-vertex provider, reusing the
# Vertex ADC + ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID above (NO API key). NOTE: OpenClaw 2026.7.x
# does NOT auto-detect metadata-server ADC — its auth gate needs a registered provider
# profile first, so the openclaw entrypoint registers a keyless Vertex ADC *marker*
# profile (see e2e/agents/openclaw/entrypoint.sh). google-auth-library then resolves
# credentials at request time: the GCE metadata server on CI (the attached service
# account) or, locally, the gcloud ADC file you mount via SAGE_E2E_GCP_ADC above
# — no key needed either way. Defaults to the `global` endpoint (matching the Claude
# path) — verify the project serves gemini-2.5-flash; override for a region.
# OPENCLAW_VERTEX_LOCATION=global
# Optionally override the model (a Vertex Gemini id; default google-vertex/gemini-2.5-flash):
# OPENCLAW_E2E_MODEL=google-vertex/gemini-2.5-flash
# Throwaway token guarding the localhost test gateway (default: sage-e2e):
# OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=sage-e2e
# Host port the containerized gateway publishes to (default: 18889). Distinct from
# OpenClaw's default 18789 so it won't collide with a local dev gateway; change it if
# 18889 is taken too.
# OPENCLAW_HOST_PORT=18889

# --- VS Code (e2e/run.sh vscode) — wiring-only Extension Host under Xvfb ---
# NO secrets required. This runs the Sage extension in a real VS Code Extension Host and
# verifies wiring (activation + enableProtection writes ~/.copilot/hooks/hooks.json + the
# canary deny matrix). It does NOT authenticate or drive Copilot Chat — that's impossible
# headless (Chat is gated behind interactive GitHub sign-in + a Copilot entitlement), so
# real-Chat tool/payload drift validation lives in Layer 3 (desktop). See e2e/README.md.
# The VS Code build version is pinned in e2e/agents.json (downloaded via @vscode/test-electron).
#
# VS Code source at image-build time: locally, leave this unset and the pinned build is
# downloaded from Microsoft's CDN. Where that CDN is unreachable (e.g. a restricted CI
# network), set this to an apt mirror of packages.microsoft.com/repos/code and VS Code is
# apt-installed instead (the pinned version is not honored on that path). Kept out of
# version control, like BASE_IMAGE.
# VSCODE_APT_MIRROR=<registry-host>/packages.microsoft.com-repos-code
